        <!-- post -->
        <div id="post-749" class="post-749 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-scrum">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/a-reminder-of-our-values/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: A Reminder Of Our Values">A Reminder Of Our Values</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Oct</span>
            <span class="day">28</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/scrum/" title="View all posts in Scrum" rel="category tag">Scrum</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/a-reminder-of-our-values/#respond" class="comments"  title="Comment on A Reminder Of Our Values"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="749 http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2009/10/a-reminder-of-our-values/">No Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>Steve Gentile recently had a thinking out loud moment by posting the Agile Manifest as a reminder to himself of what he values.&#160; It’s really important to constantly put these types of reminders in front of ourselves as we work in environments that don’t necessarily breed best practices.&#160; The contractual obligations of the business world [...]</p>

                    </div>
        </div>
        <!-- /post -->
        
        <!-- post -->
        <div id="post-744" class="post-744 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-scrum">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/size-versus-duration/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Size versus Duration">Size versus Duration</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Oct</span>
            <span class="day">27</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/scrum/" title="View all posts in Scrum" rel="category tag">Scrum</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/size-versus-duration/#respond" class="comments"  title="Comment on Size versus Duration"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="744 http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2009/10/size-versus-duration/">No Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>Scrum introduces the concept of Story Points which most teams immediately misunderstand or discard.  The most elegant wrong explanation I’ve heard for not using story points was: “we never liked story points, because then we had to communicate and teach our customers a whole new currency.”  Fortunately, this isn’t true.  Unforunately, the reason many find [...]</p>

                    </div>
        </div>
